  "term": "dialectical behavior therapy",
  "definition": "Dialectical behavior therapy is a flexible, stage-based form of therapy that draws on behavior therapy, cognitive behavior therapy, and mindfulness. It aims to support both acceptance and change at the same time, particularly for people who are hard to treat.",
